# Reviewed, justified exceptions. Each is a deliberate design decision — not an
# oversight. Triaging findings (rather than blindly suppressing them) is the point.

# KSV0014 — "root filesystem is not read-only" on postgres.
# The database engine must write to its data directory, so a read-only root
# filesystem is not possible for this container. It is still hardened: runs
# non-root (999), drops ALL capabilities, no-new-privileges, seccomp
# RuntimeDefault, a dedicated PVC for data, and /var/run/postgresql as emptyDir.
AVD-KSV-0014

# KSV0013 — ":latest" image tag.
# The dev base intentionally uses a locally-built `capstone-api:latest`. The prod
# overlay (k8s/overlays/prod) repoints it to an immutable, registry-hosted tag.
AVD-KSV-0013
